  "term": "water on the brain",
  "definition": "Water on the brain is an older popular name for hydrocephalus, an abnormal buildup of fluid inside the skull. In developed cases it was described as often beginning at birth or in early infancy, causing an enlarged head and being associated with mental dullness, reduced mental activity, and weakness.",
